# ThreadSanitizer suppressions file for mscpp tests
#
# This file suppresses known acceptable data races in test code that do not
# reflect production usage patterns.

# IOAdapterTest stress test: Concurrent port writes
# The stress test intentionally creates concurrent writes to InputPort::set()
# from multiple threads to verify that the IOAdapter's action scheduling queue
# is thread-safe under extreme conditions. This does NOT reflect production usage:
#
# Production pattern (thread-safe):
#   I/O thread → scheduleLogicalAction() → reactor thread writes ports
#
# Test pattern (intentional race for stress testing):
#   Multiple threads → simulateExternalEvent() → concurrent port writes
#
# The test validates that even with intentional concurrent port writes (which
# should never happen in production), the action scheduling mechanism remains
# thread-safe and all actions are properly queued.
race:services::InputPort<int>::set
race:MockIOAdapter::simulateExternalEvent
